---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Patterns"
  section="patterns"
  description="Best-practice ways to handle common tasks in government services, composed from the components."
>
  <section class="govbb-width-container govbb-page-section">
    <div class="govbb-page-header">
      <h1 class="govbb-page-title">Patterns</h1>
      <p class="govbb-page-subtitle">
        Best-practice ways to handle common tasks in government services,
        composed from the components.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="govbb-prose">
      <p>
        Patterns document how to combine components into a proven solution for a
        whole task, such as asking for an address or confirming a decision. We
        have not published any yet.
      </p>
      <p>
        In the meantime, start from the
        <a href="/components/">components</a>. Anything that is a single
        component, rather than a multi-step flow, lives there — including
        <a href="/components/payment/">payment</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
